Description: drm: Test a new output configuration without a stereo pair's shared buffer
 The second output of a stereo pair scans out its partner's buffer. The
 test of a new configuration kept that buffer on its primary layer, so
 changing the mode of a paired pair tested the old, smaller frame against
 the new mode's eye and the kernel refused it ("No space left on device"
 from the source rectangle check). The pair could not change mode.
 .
 Test with the layer's own buffer, as for every other output.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: https://github.com/Sparky-OS/kwin/commit/dbbc34b396df55466e37642f73e9b359d03ab88d
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-22
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 src/backends/drm/drm_gpu.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/backends/drm/drm_gpu.cpp b/src/backends/drm/drm_gpu.cpp
index 2ef7cd7..b8fa916 100644
--- a/src/backends/drm/drm_gpu.cpp
+++ b/src/backends/drm/drm_gpu.cpp
@@ -503,7 +503,8 @@ DrmPipeline::Error DrmGpu::testPipelines()
                 layer->setTargetRect(Rect(QPoint(0, 0), pipeline->mode()->size()));
                 layer->setSourceRect(Rect(QPoint(0, 0), pipeline->mode()->size()));
                 layer->setEnabled(true);
-                // ensure we have suitable buffers for the test
+                // ensure we have suitable buffers for the test, not the buffer of a stereo pair's partner
+                layer->clearSharedBuffer();
                 if (!layer->preparePresentationTest()) {
                     return DrmPipeline::Error::InvalidArguments;
                 }
